  },
  "dcim": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "the input is one power port from the cord part and each outlet a power outlet it feeds. C13 and C19 export as the IEC types; the CEE plug and the earthing-pin socket export as `other` with a label, because no upstream type for either has been read from a held source."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the front view of page 21, mm from the foot end: the foot cell 0 to 72.1 with the gland; phase 1, 72.1 to 522.8 (450.7); a spacer to 547.7 (24.9); phase 2, 547.7 to 998.7 (451); a spacer to 1023.6 (24.9); phase 3, 1023.6 to 1474.5 (450.9); a blank cell to 1477.8 (3.3); the head cap, 1477.8 to 1494, with its ribs. The cells are the ones this page draws, and no other page's. Each outlet stands in its cell as the DK 7979.175 model places it: the C13 long axis across the strip with the earth side toward the head, the C19 long axis along the strip with its earth slot toward the left of the face, the earthing-pin socket with its contact holes on one diagonal. Outlets count from the foot."
  },
  "input": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - dri1308088en p.1: \"Input voltage range (L - N) 230 V (400 V, 3~), 50 - 60 Hz\", \"Input current 16 A/32 A (depending on product variant)\", \"No. of wires 3/5\", \"Connection cable type H05-VV\", \"Length of connection cable 3m\"; the table: 3~, 16 A, 11 kW, input CEE. The circuit diagram draws the neutral to each phase group, so each outlet is line to neutral: `input-wiring: wye`. The unit has a fixed cord and no inlet. `plug-rating-a` is not written: the data sheet rates the unit, not the plug."
  },
